      "applicability": "not_applicable",
      "direction": "neutral_or_unclear",
      "decision_effect": "no_change",
      "card_ids": ["C26", "C29", "C34"]
    }
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct oral bioavailability measurement for the query molecule (bromocriptine-type) in the supplied cards.",
    "No matched oral vs IV AUC for the query or for DHEC; the low-exposure conclusion relies on very low Cmax after substantial oral doses rather than a direct F value.",
    "The DHE MAP0004 record is formulation-specific and not a conventional oral bioavailability measurement.",
    "No dose, formulation, or prandial-state data for the query.",
    "The physicochemical prior is mixed/unclear and does not independently resolve the threshold."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "L3 adds structurally relevant ergot-alkaloid oral exposure records: DHEC shows only pg/mL-level Cmax after 10–20 mg oral doses, supporting low F for this brominated ergopeptine class. The earlier high prediction relied on unrelated molecules (vinorelbine, naldemedine), and the DHE MAP0004 ratio is formulation-specific. Prediction flipped to low with moderate confidence."
}

